                <pb facs="1032" n="918" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg918"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.001 Montero, Juan/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-16T10:00:00-04:00">November 16, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 16—10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>139. Montero reassumed Vice Presidency yesterday. Balmaceda, Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs; Izquierdo, Minister of Hacienda.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
